# MVS 3.8j TK5 (Update 5) — TSO logon through ISPF and back out.
# Captured 2026-08-18 against localhost:3271 with `-model 3278-2-E`, using the
# stage 2a client (Query Reply + configurable terminal type). THE FIRST RUN THAT
# REACHES TSO: stage 1 died here with IKT00405I SCREEN ERASURE.
#
# What this proves, and what it does not:
#   * ISPF primary option menu reached (USERID: HERC02, TERMINAL: 3277), then a
#     clean logoff back to the VTAM Logon panel. 0 errors, 0 program checks.
#   * TERMINAL: 3277 and the status lines' "24 80" confirm the session stayed
#     24x80 throughout. TSO did NOT need a larger screen, and never asked for
#     one -- the 27x132 in the earlier zti capture was zti advertising its own
#     window size, not a TSO requirement.
#   * The three-unit Query Reply (Summary, Usable Area, Implicit Partition) was
#     ACCEPTED by this host. The "minimum acceptable subset is untested" caveat
#     on tso-query-reply.txt is now tested, for this host and this path.
#   * SA orders: 113 across the session. MF orders: 0. So TK5's ISPF does use
#     Set Attribute (which we parse and drop, losing only colour/highlighting)
#     and does NOT use Modify Field -- meaning stage 2a's MF deferral cost
#     nothing here. That was measured, not assumed; the counters were proven
#     able to report a presence before this run trusted their absence.
#
# REDACTED: the password appears twice in a raw capture and BOTH are removed
# here -- once as EBCDIC on the wire (c3 e4 d3 f8 e3 d9 -> 00 x6, line ~949) and
# once as PLAINTEXT in a ScreenText dump, because MVS 3.8j echoes the password to
# the screen with no masking (-> XXXXXX, line ~222). Re-record with care: the
# second one is easy to miss.
#
# Credentials are in TK5's own manual (doc/MVS_TK4-_v100_Users_Manual.pdf);
# HERC02/CUL8TR was used. Log off properly or the next run draws IKJ56425I
# LOGON REJECTED ... IN USE, which is NOT the IKT00405I failure and has been
# misscored as one before.
U U U N N 2 24 80 0 0 0x0 0.000
ok
